// What the fold passes round a cycle of imports do NOT make, and how each is
// reported.
//
// Name-resolution stage. A cycle of imports is legal, and a re-export travels
// round one: the folds run pass after pass until a pass binds nothing new
// (module-import-cycle). Until then nothing that might yet arrive is reported
// missing, so a name that never arrives is reported once, by the pass after the
// last, with the message it always had -- judged against the module once it is
// complete. A collision is final as soon as it is met, and it too is reported
// once, where a single pass would have met it.
//
// The subfolders are drawn in sorted order and their folds start in that order:
//   gamma/gamma.cone         shared, more, extra; in no cycle
//   hush/hush.cone           hidden; in no cycle
//   alpha/alpha.cone         imports beta, then re-exports gamma's shared
//   beta/beta.cone           a listed clause of alpha naming a name alpha never has
//   kappa/kappa.cone         imports lambda and nu, then re-exports more and extra
//                            and folds hush's hidden privately
//   lambda/lambda.cone       'pub use * but' of kappa: a late name and a name
//                            kappa never has
//   nu/nu.cone               a listed clause of kappa naming its private hidden
//   delta/delta.cone         a shared of its own, a different declaration
//   echo/echo.cone           imports fox and foxtail, then re-exports delta's shared
//   fox/fox.cone             echo's wildcard, then gamma's shared: the collision
//   foxtail/foxtail.cone     gamma's shared, then echo's wildcard: the collision
//   quiet/quiet.cone         imports gamma and re-exports nothing, in no cycle
//   solo/solo.cone           folds from quiet a name quiet has not got
//   solitary/solitary.cone   a wildcard 'pub use' of quiet, and a bare use of that name
//   omega/omega.cone         lists gamma's shared through psi, late, and from gamma: written twice
//   psi/psi.cone             imports omega back and re-exports all it shows
//   rho/rho.cone             the same through sigma's wildcard: never written twice, so one binding
//   sigma/sigma.cone         imports rho back and re-exports all it shows

fn reach() i64 {
  // Every fold has settled before any body resolves, so a path from outside
  // the cycle reaches what alpha re-exported ...
  alpha.shared();

  // ... and what lambda's wildcard carried on, once kappa had it
  lambda.more();

  // lambda's 'but' left extra out, though kappa did not have it the first time
  // lambda read it
  lambda.extra();           //~ ErrorUnkName:10 "The name extra does not refer to a declared name"

  // The control: quiet never re-exported shared, and no cycle is involved
  solitary.shared();        //~ ErrorUnkName:12 "The name shared does not refer to a declared name"
  0i64;
}
